FAQ = [
 ("What is the best LED light bar for a 2024–2026 Tacoma?",
  "For most trucks, Cali Raised LED's 32 in Lo Pro grille kit. Cali Raised lists it for 2024+ Tacomas, all trims except the Limited with its chrome bumper, as a bolt-on with no drilling, with laser-cut brackets that sit the bar flush to the bumper for full light exposure. One bar costs $384.99 and two cost $669.99 on the maker's site. Trucks with the 360-degree camera system can take only one bar. If you'd rather light the trail edges than the road ahead, a ditch light kit is the cheaper first step."),
 ("Does the TRD Pro or Trailhunter already have a light bar?",
  "Yes, both have factory LED lighting. Toyota's 2024 Tacoma press release says the TRD Pro gets a new integrated LED light bar that works with the LED headlights to optimize beam pattern aiming, plus RIGID white LED fog lamps. The Trailhunter gets an integrated 20 in LED light bar and white/yellow color-switching RIGID LED fog lamps, and it comes pre-wired for accessories with three auxiliary toggle switches on the dashboard. On those trims, ditch lights add more new coverage than a second grille bar."),
 ("Do 2016–2023 Tacoma light bar brackets fit the 2024–2026 Tacoma?",
  "No. The 2024–2026 Tacoma is built on Toyota's TNGA-F body-on-frame platform, shared with the Tundra, per Wikipedia, and has an all-new front end. Cali Raised sells separate 2024+ grille and ditch brackets and says its 2024 ditch brackets are not compatible with 2023 or older Tacomas. Bars and pods are universal and can move between trucks, but buy brackets titled for the 2024+ truck only."),
 ("Are LED light bars legal on a Tacoma?",
  "Usually only off-road. Rules vary by state, but many states treat light bars and auxiliary lights with off-road beam patterns as off-road equipment that must be switched off on public roads, and some also require an opaque cover or limit how many auxiliary lamps you can run and how high they sit. That applies to aftermarket grille bars and ditch pods alike. Factory lighting fitted by Toyota is a separate matter. Check your own state's vehicle code before driving with an add-on light uncovered."),
 ("Will a grille light bar work with the 360 camera on a 2024 Tacoma?",
  "With limits. Cali Raised says trucks with 360 camera systems can accommodate only one light bar in its Lo Pro grille kit, not the two it otherwise supports, and that the upper mount may need modification to the grille shutters to prevent interference. It also lists the kit as not compatible with Limited grille models. If your truck has a front camera or grille shutters, read the install notes before ordering, and after installation check that the camera view and any dash warnings are normal."),
 ("Do I need to drill to add lights to a 4th-gen Tacoma?",
  "Not with the kits on this page. Cali Raised describes its Lo Pro grille kit as bolt-on with no modifications required and no drilling, apart from possible shutter modification for the upper mount. Its ditch bracket kit and bracket-only set are listed as bolt-on at existing factory mounting points with no drilling, taking about one to two hours with basic hand tools. RealTruck describes Diode Dynamics' Stage Series ditch kits as using factory mounting points with no cutting or drilling."),
 ("How do I wire ditch lights or a light bar on a 2024 Tacoma?",
  "Use a harness with a relay, an inline fuse and a switch. Cali Raised says its complete ditch kits include a wiring harness with an integrated relay, and it sells a Toyota OEM square-style 'DITCH LIGHTS' switch for $19.99 that fits the factory dash. On a Trailhunter, Toyota says the truck is pre-wired for accessories with three auxiliary switches on the dashboard, which can simplify the job; follow the harness maker's instructions for connecting to it. Keep wires away from hood hinge travel and exhaust heat."),
 ("How many amps will a 4th-gen Tacoma light setup draw?",
  "Divide watts by system voltage. Cali Raised's ditch kits use 18 W pods or 27 W side-projecting pods, so a pair of 27 W pods draws roughly 3.9 A at 13.8 V. A 32 in dual-row bar draws considerably more, and running two bars plus ditch pods can pass 15 A. Add up every light on each circuit and size fuses and relays for that total, or give each light group its own relay and fuse."),
 ("What are side-projecting ditch light pods?",
  "They are pods built to throw light forward and to the side at the same time. Cali Raised's 4th-gen Tacoma buyer's guide recommends its 27 W side-projecting pods, saying standard forward-facing pods have to be angled outward on the bracket, which splits their light between forward and side coverage. A side-projecting pod avoids that trade-off. Standard 3x2 pods at 18 W in white (6000K) or amber (3000K) are the cheaper option in the same kit."),
 ("Can I put a light bar on the roof of a 2024 Tacoma?",
  "Usually on a roof rack or platform, not directly on the roof, and we didn't find a roof-specific bracket titled for the 4th gen with specs we could verify. A roof bar gives the most reach but also the most glare off the hood and the most wind noise, and it is off-road lighting in practically every state. Low grille bars and ditch pods avoid those trade-offs. If you plan a roof rack anyway, choose one whose front crossbar or fairing is designed to carry a bar."),
]

